WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.587
Cab and Directions.

2
00:00:01.867 --> 00:00:05.878
Day 30 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:07.628 --> 00:00:08.652
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.932 --> 00:00:10.980
Confirm, clarify, stay safe.

5
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.759
Short, clear phrases work best with drivers and strangers.

6
00:00:16.109 --> 00:00:16.962
Part 1.

7
00:00:17.242 --> 00:00:18.821
Booking or starting a ride.

8
00:00:20.071 --> 00:00:21.820
Hi, are you here for Ashish?

9
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.508
Going to Terminal 2?

10
00:00:23.788 --> 00:00:25.879
(confirm the driver before you get in).

11
00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:27.737
Can you follow the map, please?

12
00:00:28.017 --> 00:00:29.959
How long will it take with this traffic?

13
00:00:30.239 --> 00:00:32.457
Could you turn the AC up or down, please?

14
00:00:32.737 --> 00:00:34.145
Could you stop here, please?

15
00:00:34.425 --> 00:00:35.791
Just after the signal.

16
00:00:36.071 --> 00:00:37.543
Could you wait 5 minutes?

17
00:00:37.823 --> 00:00:39.231
I need to pick up a bag.

18
00:00:40.581 --> 00:00:41.455
Part 2.

19
00:00:41.735 --> 00:00:43.741
Taxi without an app (fixed fare).

20
00:00:44.991 --> 00:00:46.761
How much to the railway station?

21
00:00:47.041 --> 00:00:48.300
Do you use the meter?

22
00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:49.647
That seems high.

23
00:00:49.927 --> 00:00:51.825
Could you do 300 rupees?

24
00:00:53.175 --> 00:00:54.071
Part 3.

25
00:00:54.351 --> 00:00:55.759
Asking for directions.

26
00:00:57.009 --> 00:00:57.948
You could say:

27
00:00:58.228 --> 00:01:00.297
Excuse me, sorry to bother you.

28
00:01:00.577 --> 00:01:02.583
How do I get to the Central Library?

29
00:01:02.863 --> 00:01:04.271
Is it walking distance?

30
00:01:05.621 --> 00:01:06.965
Here is a quick table:

31
00:01:07.245 --> 00:01:08.674
Ask, and Useful when.

32
00:01:08.954 --> 00:01:10.191
Is it far from here?:

33
00:01:10.471 --> 00:01:12.135
Deciding walk versus cab.

34
00:01:12.415 --> 00:01:14.399
Which way is the metro station?:

35
00:01:14.679 --> 00:01:15.746
Need a direction.

36
00:01:16.026 --> 00:01:17.711
Is there a bus that goes there?:

37
00:01:17.991 --> 00:01:19.229
Public transport.

38
00:01:19.509 --> 00:01:20.895
Can you show me on the map?:

39
00:01:21.175 --> 00:01:22.903
Directions are complicated.

40
00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:25.167
So, straight, then left at the bank.

41
00:01:25.447 --> 00:01:26.173
Right?:

42
00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:28.010
Confirming (repeat back!).

43
00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:39.237
Direction vocabulary: go straight, turn left or right, take the second left, at the signal or roundabout, opposite, next to, around the corner, cross the road.

44
00:01:40.587 --> 00:01:41.505
Part 4.

45
00:01:41.785 --> 00:01:43.001
Safety phrases.

46
00:01:44.251 --> 00:01:47.003
Please don't take a different route without asking me.

47
00:01:47.283 --> 00:01:49.800
I'm sharing my live location with my family.

48
00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.360
Please stop the car.

49
00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:52.941
I'd like to get out here.

50
00:01:54.291 --> 00:01:55.251
Part 5.

51
00:01:55.531 --> 00:01:56.961
Practice conversations.

52
00:01:58.211 --> 00:01:59.683
Talking to the cab driver.

53
00:01:59.963 --> 00:02:01.989
Here is how the conversation goes.

54
00:02:02.269 --> 00:02:03.635
Hello, Ashish sir?

55
00:02:03.915 --> 00:02:04.619
Yes.

56
00:02:04.899 --> 00:02:07.992
Are you going to Terminal 2, Kempegowda Airport?

57
00:02:08.272 --> 00:02:09.552
Yes, please sit.

58
00:02:09.832 --> 00:02:11.731
Could you follow the map, please?

59
00:02:12.011 --> 00:02:14.059
There's usually traffic at Hebbal.

60
00:02:14.339 --> 00:02:15.448
Okay.

61
00:02:15.728 --> 00:02:17.413
Should I take the toll road?

62
00:02:18.763 --> 00:02:20.363
The conversation continues.

63
00:02:20.643 --> 00:02:21.945
Yes, that's fine.

64
00:02:22.225 --> 00:02:23.633
I'll pay the toll.

65
00:02:23.913 --> 00:02:25.406
How long will it take?

66
00:02:25.686 --> 00:02:27.307
About 55 minutes.

67
00:02:27.587 --> 00:02:29.593
My flight is at 9:30.

68
00:02:29.873 --> 00:02:32.710
Could you please drive a bit faster, but safely?

69
00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:35.230
Don't worry, we'll reach by 8:15.

70
00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:36.449
Thank you.

71
00:02:36.729 --> 00:02:38.905
Could you turn the AC down a little?

72
00:02:40.255 --> 00:02:42.217
Asking a stranger for directions.

73
00:02:42.497 --> 00:02:44.524
Here is how the conversation goes.

74
00:02:44.804 --> 00:02:47.129
Excuse me, sorry to bother you.

75
00:02:47.409 --> 00:02:49.543
Do you know where the City Library is?

76
00:02:49.823 --> 00:02:51.252
Yes, it's not far.

77
00:02:51.532 --> 00:02:53.815
Go straight for about 200 metres.

78
00:02:54.095 --> 00:02:55.375
Okay, straight.

79
00:02:55.655 --> 00:02:57.596
At the traffic signal, turn left.

80
00:02:57.876 --> 00:03:00.649
It's the second building on your right, opposite the bank.

81
00:03:01.999 --> 00:03:03.599
The conversation continues.

82
00:03:03.879 --> 00:03:08.103
So, straight, left at the signal, and it's on the right, opposite the bank?

83
00:03:08.383 --> 00:03:09.365
Exactly.

84
00:03:09.645 --> 00:03:11.543
It's about five minutes on foot.

85
00:03:11.823 --> 00:03:13.231
Thank you so much!

86
00:03:13.511 --> 00:03:14.514
You're welcome.

87
00:03:15.864 --> 00:03:17.400
That's the end of this lesson.

88
00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:22.331
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

89
00:03:22.611 --> 00:03:28.733
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

